  "live_records": {
    "q-77143": {
      "dom_id": "step-q77143",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14284597/assets/801321d1639e668c3778c198df9a5b98ea3e6018f12ab2e5c756bfa4f04cb574.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $C$ is the closed polygonal path $OGHO,$ shown in the diagram above, traversed in the counterclockwise direction?",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that we can represent $C,$ which is traversed in counterclockwise, as the union of $3$ paths:\n\n$$\nC=\\{-{C}_{1}\\}\\cup \\{-{C}_{2}\\}\\cup {C}_{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $-{C}_{1}$ and $-{C}_{2}$ are the same paths as ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ but traversed in the opposite direction.\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{-{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r-{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
